# P-20260923-097: wire KG status string into the approved/rejected booleans rank() reads
# Source: swarm-05 MEMORY-TRACE.md M2 "wiring gap (secondary finding)" + CONVERGED-PIPELINE.md
# gap table (RETRIEVAL row).
# Target repo: /home/nolan/ping (live gateway tree).
# Anchor: ping-runtime/search/hybrid_search.js, knowledge-graph context leg, results.push({...}).
# The KG leg pushes `status: node.status` (string) but never sets the `approved`/`rejected`
# booleans that EvidenceAuthority.rank() reads (approved x1.2 boost, rejected x0.2 penalty).
# Today both are dead code for KG results and ranking falls back to confidence alone
# (1.0 vs 0.5 still orders approved above candidate, which is why the existing F1 test
# passes despite the dead path). The 5-line addition makes rank() honor its contract.
# The semantic leg needs no change: it already sets `verified` from the evidence trace
# (verify()) and rank() handles its fields.
# Known adjacent seam (not in scope, flagged): the KG leg hardcodes `verified: true`
# ("stored node - already passed the graph write path") instead of tracing source_event_id
# back to ping_events the way the semantic leg does. Rank math is unaffected; the
# assembler (P-20260923-098) treats verified as a strict boolean either way.
# Test: unit-test the KG-leg push shape with a stubbed knowledgeGraph (assert
# approved/rejected booleans track node.status), then rank() orders an approved node
# above a candidate at equal confidence.
# ---
--- a/ping-runtime/search/hybrid_search.js
+++ b/ping-runtime/search/hybrid_search.js
@@ -98,6 +98,12 @@
             verified: true, // stored node — already passed the graph write path
             source: 'knowledge',
             status: node.status,
+            // swarm-05 (I1/I3): wire the status string into the booleans
+            // EvidenceAuthority.rank() reads (approved x1.2, rejected x0.2).
+            // Without these the approval boost and rejection penalty are dead
+            // code for KG results and ranking falls back to confidence alone.
+            approved: node.status === 'approved',
+            rejected: node.status === 'rejected',
             node_type: node.node_type,
             label: node.label,
             entity_id: node.entity_id,
